INVARIANCE: a collinear consecutive triple survives every defined AKR shift.
  Shift of side k replaces Z_k by a point of aff(Z_{k-1},Z_k) and Z_{k+1} by a
  point of aff(Z_{k+1},Z_{k+2}); both LINES are unchanged.  A collinear triple
  (k-2,k-1,k) lies in aff(Z_{k-1},Z_k), so its moved member stays on it;
  likewise (k+1,k+2,k+3).  The triples (k-1,k,k+1) and (k,k+1,k+2) cannot be
  collinear, since that is exactly (NC) and the shift would be undefined.
  Shifts of the OTHER polygon do not move Z at all.

